# A choice's case that holds a blueprint, in a module that emits a row variable (Type
# System ch. 2, "Rows in `emit` and in signatures": a blueprint type with no `emit` of its
# own emits the row of the scope it is written in, and a module's `emit r` is "a variable
# of each signature in it, quantified per signature"): a choice is no signature and has no
# row of its own to quantify, as a record has none (neg/record-blueprint-field-row-
# variable), so the case's row would be a variable nothing binds. A case that writes its
# row with `emit` is fine. The expected text is derived by hand from the book. Written by
# Claude on the claude-bugs branch; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
mod Cards
use Ui.*

@main: @unit
@main:
    Ui.Label($text=$"x")
